<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">October 4, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 219 of the 2026 Iran War</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-10-04T07:00:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45 · Sunday cold-start audit</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Diplomatic track in hard freeze as Rubio expelled Iran's UNGA delegation — <span class="cite">F7</span> (ceasefire by Oct 27) at 9% — while three US carriers in theater and Trump's midterm deadline keep escalation material: <span class="cite">F9</span> at 32% for major strikes Nov 4–15.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- 2. FORECAST BOARD -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">5 active · Sunday cold-start audit · last reasoned 2026-10-04</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-term · ≤72h</div>

      <!-- F6: Iran-US indirect session by Oct 7 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a confirmed Iran-US indirect negotiating session occur before EOD 2026-10-07?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">10%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New · 2026-10-04</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-07</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 72h forecast. After UNGA-margin session (Sep 23) and Iran's Sep 24 roadmap submission, US Secretary Rubio expelled the Iranian diplomatic delegation. Trump described post-midterm military action as a live option. Pakistan and Qatar channels are intact but no session is currently scheduled. A confirmed session within 72 hours is low-probability given the expulsion of Iranian envoys and publicly hardened positions.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Reuters/AP/AFP or named mediator confirms a meeting between US and Iranian officials — direct or through identified intermediaries — before EOD Oct 7. Pure message relay: NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP, or official statement from either government or named mediator (Qatar, Pakistan, Oman MFA).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Meeting reported but either side later denies it: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Phone calls without face-to-face or direct written exchange: NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar MFA announces session</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Rubio/Witkoff travel to Qatar or Oman within 48h</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 days</div>

      <!-- F5: Likud plurality Oct 27 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud win the most Knesset seats (seat plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −4pp from 42% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Sunday cold-start audit. Five late-September polls: Eisenkot's Yashar averaging 23.6 seats vs Likud 21.8 (Jerusalem Post; Haaretz Oct 1); Yashar leads in four of five polls. Israel Supreme Court (Oct 2) reinstated Ra'am and Joint List for the Oct 27 election. Cold-start p_cold=0.32 (party polling ahead at T-25 days wins plurality in ~75% of Israeli elections; Yashar leads four of five). Judge partial cold-start credit: war-context incumbency effect and historical right-wing polling undercount applied. Published p=0.38.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Central Elections Committee results show Likud winning more seats than any other single party in the Oct 27 election.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Israeli Central Elections Committee official results, carried by Times of Israel/Haaretz/Reuters/AP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Likud ties another party on seats: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Exit polls alone do not resolve; official preliminary results suffice if before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">Polls showing Likud ≥23 seats, ahead of Yashar</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud bloc forms coalition-eligible alliance pre-election</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Eisenkot/Yashar polling surge &gt;25 seats</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F7: US-Iran ceasefire by Oct 27 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F7</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the United States and Iran announce a formal ceasefire or binding temporary truce before EOD 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">9%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New · 2026-10-04</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 23-day forecast. Talks stalled after the UNGA session: Iranian delegation expelled from US territory; gap between Iran's 60-day-halt roadmap and US conditions not closed. Trump described post-midterm military action as a live option. Three US carrier groups in theater as of October 3. Previous ceasefire cycles took 4-6 weeks of active talks; 23 days to a binding ceasefire with no session scheduled is very low probability.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if both governments (or named senior officials) jointly announce or individually confirm a ceasefire, truce, or hostilities halt ≥24h before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Official government statement (White House, Iranian Presidency, or MFA) plus Reuters/AP/AFP wire confirmation.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Unilateral announcement without other side's confirmation: NO. Lebanon-only ceasefire without Iran-US component: NO. 'Pause for negotiations' with no specific duration and no named start time: NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar/Pakistan MFA convenes US-Iran session before Oct 20</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump endorses Iran's Sep 24 roadmap framework</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F8: Hormuz >=20/day by Oct 31 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the 7-day rolling average of AIS-visible commercial vessel transits through the Strait of Hormuz reach ≥20 vessels/day before EOD 2026-10-31?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New · 2026-10-04</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 27-day forecast. Week of Sep 23-30: ~17 vessels/day 7-day AIS average. Straits.live showed Strait "Closed" Oct 2 (Day 217). USS Theodore Roosevelt arrived Oct 3, expanding US presence to three carrier groups; IRGC mine-threat not neutralized. Prior F4 (≥30/day by Oct 3) resolved NO. Resets threshold to 20/day (24% of pre-war baseline); slow drift upward possible if no new escalation.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if any credible maritime tracker (straits.live, UANI, IMF PortWatch, Windward AI) reports a 7-consecutive-day average ≥20 AIS-visible commercial vessel transits through Hormuz before EOD Oct 31.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Straits.live daily brief, UANI Iran Shipping Update, or Windward AI. At least two sources consistent if both available.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Only one source reports ≥20 while others show &lt;20: flag AMBIGUOUS. US Navy escort convoys excluded from commercial transit count.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Straits.live reports ≥20 commercial vessels on a single day</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC announces suspension of Hormuz interdiction</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 days</div>

      <!-- F9: US major strikes Nov 4-15 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the United States initiate a new major wave of air or naval strikes against Iranian military targets between 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">32%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New · 2026-10-04</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-11-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 42-day forecast. Trump explicitly stated post-midterm military action is a live option if negotiations fail. Iranian negotiators expelled from US in early October. Three US carrier groups in theater as of October 3. The November 3 US midterms are an explicit political decision node: Trump conditioned resumed military operations on that date. Countervailing: Pakistan and Qatar mediation channels intact; Iran's Sep 24 roadmap not formally withdrawn.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM press release or Reuters/AP/AFP confirms at least two distinct US strike packages against named Iranian military facilities, vessels, or IRGC assets in the Nov 4-15 window, with at least one strike in Iran's territorial waters or mainland Iran.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM official press release plus Reuters/AP/AFP. Does not resolve on Iranian claims alone.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Strikes against Houthi or Iranian-proxy targets outside Iran proper: NO. Iranian state-media claims without CENTCOM confirmation: NO. Single isolated strike: NO — requires at least two distinct named packages.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump announces post-midterm military ultimatum with specific deadline</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US-Iran ceasefire agreement before Nov 3</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Fourth US carrier strike group ordered to Persian Gulf</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 months</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. 24-48H DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>The September 2 kinetic exchange — Iranian missiles intercepted by Kuwaiti air defenses, CENTCOM strikes on IRGC launchers, Iran targeting US naval assets — gave way within 72 hours to a Pakistani-brokered de-escalation. By September 5, President Trump announced an extension of the short-term ceasefire; Iran's Supreme National Security Council publicly accepted a two-week halt and committed to a second round of talks in Islamabad. Tasnim News Agency simultaneously ran a denial — "no official position has been announced by Iran in this regard" — exposing a factional split between the Pezeshkian executive and IRGC-aligned media, but the SNSC is the authoritative constitutional body whose announcement governed resolution. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Iran's September 5 Islamabad commitment did not produce a convened session before the September 17 horizon. On September 10, Trump said talks were "possible within days" and Pakistani officials described a session as "36-72 hours away," but no Iranian delegation arrived before the deadline. The first confirmed Iran-US indirect session in this conflict cycle opened at the UN General Assembly in New York around September 23, with US envoys Witkoff and Kushner meeting Foreign Minister Araghchi through Qatari intermediaries — six days past the September 17 resolution window. Modern Diplomacy (Sep 28) framed the diplomatic contacts as newly "resuming," confirming a gap in the September 6-22 window. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>Commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz remained well below the 30-vessel/day threshold through the October 3 resolution window. The week of September 23-30 recorded 119 total AIS-visible transits — a 7-day average of approximately 17 vessels/day, against a pre-war baseline of 85/day. September 30 logged 16 transits. Straits.live classified the Strait as "Closed" on October 2 (Day 217). On October 3, the USS Theodore Roosevelt carrier strike group arrived in theater, expanding US naval presence to three carrier groups; the IRGC mine-threat and harassment posture had not been neutralized. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>Five Israeli election surveys published in the last week of September placed Eisenkot's Yashar at an average of 23.6 Knesset seats versus Likud's 21.8; Yashar leads in four of five polls, with one i24NEWS outlier giving Likud a significant margin. Bloc arithmetic stands at approximately 52-52. On October 2, Israel's Supreme Court unanimously overturned the Central Elections Committee's bans on Ra'am and the Joint List, confirming Arab-majority party participation in the October 27 election and shifting coalition formation calculus slightly toward the opposition. The Sunday cold-start audit derived p_cold=0.32 independently; Judge published p=0.38, applying partial credit for war-context incumbency and historical polling bias toward right-wing parties. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>

      <p>The diplomatic environment as of October 4 hardened following the UNGA-margin session. US Secretary Rubio ordered Iran's negotiating delegation to leave US territory after the two sides failed to close the gap between Tehran's September 24 roadmap and Washington's conditions. Trump told reporters Iran is "ready to fold up" and described post-November-3 military action as a live option if negotiations do not conclude by the midterm date. Three US carrier strike groups are now in the Persian Gulf theater. The November 3 US midterm elections constitute the next structural decision node in the conflict timeline. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. SCENARIO MAP -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
        <div class="prob-bar prob-escalation" style="width:32%;">Escalation 32%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-status" style="width:56%;">Protracted 56%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-deescalation" style="width:12%;">De-esc 12%</div>
      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (32%):</strong> With three US carriers in theater and Trump's midterm-conditional military threat (<span style="color:var(--accent);font-family:monospace;font-size:0.9em;">F9</span>), an organized post-November-3 strike campaign is the primary escalation pathway if talks remain dead through the midterm date.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (56%):</strong> The most likely outcome — ongoing naval blockade, sporadic IRGC harassment, and no ceasefire in the forecast window, as both sides hold hardened positions and await post-midterm political clarity.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (12%):</strong> A revived Pakistan or Qatar channel produces a new session before Oct 27, leading toward a ceasefire framework (<span style="color:var(--accent);font-family:monospace;font-size:0.9em;">F7</span> at 9%); requires both sides to soften publicly stated positions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. INSIDE IRAN -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · ~200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media ran a disciplined generous-peacemaker narrative across October 1-4, framing the September 24 roadmap as a "comprehensive peace framework" voluntarily offered and rejected by Washington. IRNA and the official Presidency channel attributed continued hostilities to a US "choice against peace," serving SNSC domestic credibility after the factionally costly September 5 ceasefire acceptance. PressTV's English-language broadcasts amplified official characterizations of the US rejection as proof that Washington "does not want peace." → supports <span class="cite">F7</span> without move</p>

      <p>Tasnim (IRGC-linked) diverged sharply on September 5, issuing a same-day denial of the SNSC ceasefire acceptance — a rare public display of executive-IRGC incoherence. By October 3-4, Tasnim and Fars had realigned to the state narrative, jointly characterizing the expulsion of Iranian delegates from US territory as "US diplomatic aggression" and the USS Theodore Roosevelt arrival as "strategic desperation rather than deterrent capability." Kayhan ran editorials framing the three-carrier buildup as evidence the US "has no path to victory on land." → supports <span class="cite">F9</span> without move</p>

      <p>IRNA attributed rising consumer prices and currency weakness entirely to "illegal US sanctions and blockade," with no mention of IRGC mine-laying operations as a driver of the Hormuz disruption. The Strait closure appeared in state-media framing as a defensive posture against "US naval aggression in Iranian territorial waters." IRNA's coverage of Israel's October 2 Supreme Court ruling reinstating Arab parties was minimal, framed as evidence of "Israeli democratic facade crumbling under international scrutiny." → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 6. REGIME CHANGE WATCH -->
  <div class="section" id="regime-change">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Regime Change Watch
      <span class="meta">12-month horizon · weekly review only (Sundays) · no intra-week deltas</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="regime-watch">
      <div class="regime-watch-meta">Last reviewed: <strong>2026-10-04</strong> · Next review: <strong>2026-10-11</strong></div>

      <div class="regime-row">
        <span class="name">🇮🇷 Iran (Regime Collapse)</span>
        <span class="p">12–20%</span>
        <div class="drivers">The September 5 SNSC-Tasnim split (IRGC publicly contradicting the executive) was the most visible sign of intra-regime stress since the conflict began. Economic pressure from the Hormuz closure and sustained US blockade on Iranian ports continues, with IRNA attributing price increases entirely to external causes. No evidence of large-scale street protests or military defections in open sources as of early October; regime control intact but economic legitimacy under visible strain.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="regime-row">
        <span class="name">🇮🇱 Israel (Netanyahu Steps Down)</span>
        <span class="p">10–18%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Netanyahu is in full election campaign mode for October 27; voluntary resignation is not consistent with campaign behavior. If Yashar wins plurality and Eisenkot forms a government, Netanyahu would become opposition leader — not necessarily stepping down from Likud leadership. Probability range reflects the structural pressure of a likely electoral loss (F5 at 38% for Likud plurality) combined with post-election coalition uncertainty; a prolonged opposition role could eventually produce a leadership change within 12 months.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

